    <statement><p>The figure below shows a function <m>g(x)</m> and its tangent line at the
point <m>B = (1.6,7.6)</m>.  If the point <m>A</m> on the tangent line is
<m>(1.57,7.68)</m>, fill in the blanks below to complete the statements about
the function <m>g</m> at the point <m>B</m>.</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__Michigan__Chap2Sec2__Q13_pg-image-1.png" width="41%"/>
<p><m>g(</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/> <m>) =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><m>g'(</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0003"/> <m>) =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1.6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>7.6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1.6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-1\cdot 0.08}{0.03}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>B=(1.6,7.6)</m> is on the graph of <m>g</m>, we have 
<m>g(1.6)=7.6</m>.
The slope of the tangent line touching the graph at <m>x=2</m> is given 
by 
<me>\mbox{slope} = \frac{\mbox{rise}}{\mbox{run}} = 
    \frac{7.6-7.68}{1.6-1.57} = -2.667.</me>
Thus, <m>g'(1.6)=-2.667</m>.



</solution>
